{
  "description": "Shared herdr session scoping v1 test vectors for Notification Registration entries (plugin/README.md, `session` field). Single source of truth consumed by both the Node plugin tests and the Swift app tests. `names` pins the session name rule shared by herdr (src/session.rs validate_name) and the app (HerdrSessionName.isValid): 1-64 bytes of ASCII letters, digits, `.`, `_` and `-`, excluding `.` and `..`. `derivation` maps a hook's HERDR_SOCKET_PATH (`socketPath` null means unset) to its session: \"\" for the default session, the name for a named session, null for an unknown shape. The named shape `/herdr/sessions/<valid name>/herdr.sock` is checked before the default suffix `/herdr/herdr.sock`. `delivery` lists registration entries and the indexes a hook in `ownSession` delivers to: entries without a string `session` are legacy and receive every session's deliveries; others only their exact session; an unknown session (null) delivers to legacy entries only. The literal name \"default\" is not special.",
